            "id": "ab9f01e0e0f8ec01f2132115889ff7ae35ffef5ffbdf5f201e2c1231c1381520",
            "content_html": "<p>In this meditation on community, gentrification, and erasure, Stonewall veteran and trans activist Sylvia Rivera takes up residency on the Hudson River piers with a group of HIV-positive New Yorkers, as cranes raze vacant buildings for a new skyline. </p>\n<p>An audio descriptive version of the film, narrated by filmmaker and activist Tourmaline, can be found <a target=\"_self\" href=\"https://fieldofvision.org/this-is-an-address-audio-description-tourmaline\">here</a>.</p>",
