            "id": "2eddb8f72cad27b6224b6430f63f704f1ef5a8bc778d849ac4a48ce0b5edc676",
            "content_html": "<p>Told from within the heart of the Hong Kong protests, “Do Not Split” begins in 2019 as a proposed bill allowing the Chinese government to extradite criminal suspects to mainland China escalated protests throughout Hong Kong. Unfolding across a year, “Do Not Split” captures the determination and sacrifices of the protesters, the government’s backlash, and the passage of the new Beijing-backed national security law.</p>\n<p>Directed by Anders Hammer</p>\n<p>A version of the film without audio description can be found <a target=\"_self\" href=\"https://fieldofvision.org/do-not-split\">here</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://fieldofvision.org/shorts/do-not-split-audio-description",
            "title": "Do Not Split (Audio Description)(35 min.)",
            "summary": "<p>Told from within the heart of the Hong Kong protests, “Do Not Split” begins in 2019 as a proposed bill allowing the Chinese government to extradite criminal suspects to mainland China escalated protests throughout Hong Kong. Unfolding across a year, “Do Not Split” captures the determination and sacrifices of the protesters, the government’s backlash, and the passage of the new Beijing-backed national security law.</p>\n<p>Directed by Anders Hammer</p>\n<p>A version of the film without audio description can be found <a target=\"_self\" href=\"https://fieldofvision.org/do-not-split\">here</a>.</p>",
            "image": "https://fieldofvision.org/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.sanity.io%2Fimages%2F8a7mgm6p%2Fproduction%2F9ba027d576f9e3b68c5c7bf2f86b72b95a39465b-720x406.jpg%3Frect%3D1%2C0%2C719%2C406%26w%3D340%26h%3D192%26fit%3Dcrop%26auto%3Dformat%26dpr%3D2&w=3840&q=75",
