            "id": "e30d5951f679467ecb78a0309150f1360bf238ad96765df8d6bbdb1b58eea761",
            "content_html": "<p>In 1939, New York's Madison Square Garden was host to an enormous—and shocking—gathering of 22,000 Americans that has largely been forgotten from our history.</p>\n<p>For more on the rally, read a Q&amp;A with Marshall Curry <a target=\"_self\" href=\"https://fieldofvision.org/q-a-with-a-night-at-the-garden-director-marshall-curry\">here</a>.</p>",
